  "title": "The Exit Plan Meets a Blocked Line",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A community center wants a preparedness illustration, but a single unverified arrow crosses a blocked doorway in its fictional floor plan. A qualified review replaces guesswork with an approved, accessible route plan.",
  "hook": "Who checked that this arrow leads somewhere usable?",
  "visible_action": "A route line stops at a blocked-door icon; the drawing gains a review checkpoint before any revised route is shown.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Preparedness diagrams need verified, locally appropriate routes and accessibility considerations.",
  "gate": "Require local fire and accessibility review before publication; teach no improvised evacuation tactics. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
